# Docker does NOT read .gitignore, so everything gitignored has to be repeated
# here or `COPY . .` bakes it into the image.
#
# This file is load-bearing for a CLAIM, not just for build speed: the
# Dockerfile header and docs/DEPLOYMENT.md 1c both state that data_cache/ is
# not baked into the image and must be mounted. Without this file that
# statement was false -- `COPY . .` was copying 5.3 GB of real tissue data,
# 647 MB of run history, and a 618 MB macOS virtualenv into the image.

# --- real data: mounted at runtime, never baked in (this is the claim) ---
data_cache/
.export-drive/
supp.zip

# --- writable runtime state: belongs in a volume, not a layer ---
app/runs/
app/projects/
app/reports/
app/uploads/
# app/compounds/ holds the operator's UNPUBLISHED SMILES. Dockerfile is
# `COPY . .`, so without this line every image built on a workstation ships
# that operator's compound series inside a layer -- and layers get pushed.
app/compounds/

# --- host-specific / wrong-platform ---
.venv/
venv/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# --- not needed by the server image ---
#
# NOTE: Docker only treats a line that STARTS with '#' as a comment -- there is
# no inline-comment syntax. A trailing "# ..." becomes part of the pattern, so
# `landing-3d/   # the marketing site` matches nothing and silently copies the
# directory in. That was true here until it was caught: it would have baked
# 827 MB of landing-3d/ (including node_modules/) and 169 MB of results/ into
# the image. Keep every comment on its own line.
.git/
.github/
# the marketing site is a separate Next.js app
landing-3d/
# the retired synthetic-era code
archive/
# generated reports and figures
results/
marketing/
docs/
*.md
!README.md

# --- editor / OS noise ---
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# --- agent worktrees: a SECOND COPY of the repo that defeats every rule above
#
# MEASURED, not theoretical. The first real `docker build` of this Dockerfile
# put 161 MB under /app/.claude, because .claude/worktrees/<agent-id>/ is a
# complete git worktree of this repository and none of the patterns above match
# a path with that prefix. `results/` excludes results/ -- it does NOT exclude
# .claude/worktrees/x/results/. So the image contained:
#
#   151 MB  .claude/worktrees/*/results/         (excluded at top level)
#   113 MB  .claude/worktrees/*/results/fprof/   a CHROME BROWSER PROFILE,
#           including Default/Cookies, Default/Login Data, Default/Login Data
#           For Account, Default/Web Data and Default/History -- the operator's
#           saved credentials, baked into a layer, and layers get pushed
#     plus  docs/, marketing/, landing-3d/, archive/, app/runs/ and a .git
#
# i.e. every claim the rest of this file exists to make was false by way of the
# duplicate. A worktree that happened to hold data_cache/ or app/compounds/
# would have shipped those the same way. Exclude the whole directory.
.claude/
